  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0052 database is used for a forum-like application, where users can create threads and replies, and other users can like and subscribe to these. The database contains 11 tables, each representing a different entity or relationship in the application.\nThe failed_jobs table stores information about failed jobs, including the connection, queue, payload, exception, and timestamp of when the job failed.\nThe likes table stores information about likes, including the user who liked a reply or thread, the likeable item (either a reply or thread), and the timestamp of when the like was created.\nThe migrations table stores information about database migrations, including the migration name and the batch number.\nThe notifications table stores information about notifications, including the type of notification, the notifiable entity (either a user or a thread), the data associated with the notification, and the timestamp of when the notification was created.\nThe password_resets table stores information about password resets, including the email address and the token used to reset the password.\nThe replies table stores information about replies, including the body of the reply, the author, and the timestamp of when the reply was created.\nThe subscriptions table stores information about subscriptions, including the user who subscribed to a thread or reply, the subscribable item (either a thread or reply), and the timestamp of when the subscription was created.\nThe taggables table stores information about tags, including the taggable item (either a thread or reply), the tag, and the timestamp of when the tag was created.\nThe tags table stores information about tags, including the name and slug of the tag.\nThe threads table stores information about threads, including the author, subject, body, slug, and timestamp of when the thread was created.\nThe users table stores information about users, including their GitHub ID, username, email, name, and timestamp of when the user was created.\nEach table has primary keys, foreign keys, and other constraints that enforce entity and referential integrity. For example, the likes table has foreign keys to the users and replies tables, and the subscriptions table has foreign keys to the users and threads tables. The failed_jobs table has a primary key on the id column, and the migrations table has a primary key on the id column. The notifications table has a primary key on the id column, and the password_resets table has a primary key on the email column. The replies table has a primary key on the id column, and the subscriptions table has a primary key on the uuid column. The taggables table has a primary key on the id column, and the tags table has a primary key on the id column. The threads table has a primary key on the id column, and the users table has a primary key on the id column.",
  "gold_question": "Community Portal for Laravel\n\n 1) Background / Context\nThe project involves developing a community portal powered by Laravel.io. This platform functions as a forum for Laravel enthusiasts to facilitate problem-solving, knowledge sharing, and community building. It serves as a hub for discussions, idea sharing, and assistance on Laravel-related topics.\n\n 2) Objectives\n- Provide a seamless forum experience for users to discuss Laravel-related issues.\n- Enable knowledge sharing and community engagement among Laravel enthusiasts.\n- Facilitate user interactions through features like threads, replies, and tags.\n\n 3) Stakeholders & Users\n- Laravel Enthusiasts: Primary users who participate in discussions and knowledge sharing.\n- Administrators: Manage the platform, oversee user interactions, and ensure smooth operation.\n\n 4) Functional Descriptions\n- User Registration: Users can sign up using their email or GitHub credentials.\n- Threads: Users can create threads to initiate discussions or queries.\n- Replies: Users can post replies to threads or as responses to other replies.\n- Likes: Users can like threads and replies to show appreciation or agreement.\n- Notifications: Users receive notifications related to interactions on their posts or threads they follow.\n- Tags: Threads can be tagged for categorization and improved searchability.\n- Subscriptions: Users can subscribe to threads or topics to receive updates.\n- Password Resets: Users can reset their passwords using a secure token-based system.\n\n 5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n- Scalability: The system should efficiently handle a growing number of users and posts.\n- Security: Secure authentication and authorization, with provisions for banning users when necessary.\n- Performance: The system should ensure responsive interactions and fast loading times.\n- Reliability: Provide consistent uptime and handle failed job processes effectively.\n- Usability: User-friendly interfaces for ease of use, even for those not technically proficient.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_codellama13b/0052.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0052\nCREATE TABLE `failed_jobs` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `connection` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `queue` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `payload` text NOT NULL,\n  `exception` text NOT NULL,\n  `failed_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `likes` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `likeable_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `likeable_type` enum('reply','thread') NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `user_id` (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `likes_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `migrations` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `migration` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `batch` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `notifications` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `notifiable_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `notifiable_type` enum('user','thread') NOT NULL,\n  `data` text NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `password_resets` (\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `token` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`email`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `replies` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `body` text NOT NULL,\n  `author_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `author_id` (`author_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `replies_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`author_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `subscriptions` (\n  `uuid` char(36) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `subscribable_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `subscribable_type` enum('thread','reply') NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`uuid`),\n  KEY `user_id` (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `subscriptions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `taggables` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `taggable_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `taggable_type` enum('reply','thread') NOT NULL,\n  `tag_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `tag_id` (`tag_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `taggables_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`tag_id`) REFERENCES `tags` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `tags` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `slug` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `threads` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `author_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `subject` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `body` text NOT NULL,\n  `slug` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `author_id` (`author_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `threads_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`author_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `github_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
